MOVES — the vocabulary every rung above composes, instead of reaching into lines

level 0 — the three lookups a pile answers:
    leaving(end)    lines with end as their left
    reaching(end)   lines with end as their right
    named(id)       the line an id names
    (a line's id is an end too, so "what is said about a line" is the same lookups)

level 1 — moves, each from a step {to, via line} to next steps:
    down    along any line, left → right              up      right → left
    part    down, along contains lines only           whole   up, along contains only
    left    from a reference to its line's left       right   ... to its line's right
    about   from the line just walked to what is said about it
    rule:   a move never goes back through the line it came by

level 2 — phrases, named chains of moves:
    beside   = whole part                    the other parts of each whole it is in
    is       = whole about                   what the finding lines say it is
    peers    = whole about up right          everything found as the same word
    broader  = down:<BROADER>                one step up the tower

operators, on any move or phrase:
    narrow   move:word    keep steps whose line is said to be (or said by) word
                          narrowing a phrase narrows its last move: beside:ip = whole part:ip
    repeat   move*        take it again and again, to every end not yet reached

said(line) = what is said about a line, folded:
    a reference → a word (the end of the sense that isn't its vocabulary)
    a string    → a source

walk(start, moves) = rows: each row the steps taken, the evidence for its last end
